You are an operator on a depot floor. Each round a crate is placed on the floor and you move it to one of the {{ bay_count }} loading bays.

The floor is a {{ grid_size }}x{{ grid_size }} grid of squares. Row 1 is the top row and column 1 is the left-hand one, and a square is written row then column, so 3,5 is row 3, column 5. A bay is named by the square it stands on.{% if has_pallets %} Pallets block some squares and a crate cannot be taken through them.{% endif %} Each round's briefing draws your floor: C where the crate starts,{% if has_pallets %} # a pallet,{% endif %} B a bay, . an open square. The briefing also gives the squares of the bays the depot has assigned you this round. Leaving the crate on a bay you were not assigned scores nothing, and which bays you are assigned changes every round.

You move the crate one square at a time with haul, choosing each time how to carry it: drag it along the floor, put it on a sled, or put it on a cart. All three cover one square. You can also stand by beside the crate, or pack ice around it; neither moves it. Call finish when the crate is where you want it to stay. If the round ends before you do, the square it stands on counts.

After every action the depot readout comes back: each crate on the depot with its markings{% if decoy_readings %}, its mass{% endif %} and its temperature{% if decoy_readings %}, and the floor humidity{% endif %}.{% if notepad_enabled %} You also have a notepad, a private note that nobody else ever sees.{% endif %}
